From: Nerves system for the SMT1019
Subject: [PATCH] dts: rk3576 wf1019: RGB light ring via mainline pwm-leds

The board's RGB "light ring" is three channels of pwm2 (the 8-channel block
at 0x2ade_0000): red on ch6 (pwm@2ade6000), green on ch2 (pwm@2ade2000) and
blue on ch5 (pwm@2ade5000). rk3576s-evb-r157.dtsi already enables all three
on the pwm2 "m1" pin mux and describes the LED with the out-of-tree vendor
"pwm-four-leds" driver (/dev/ledjni), which caps each channel at 16 brightness
levels and needs userspace temporal dithering for smooth fades.

Delete that vendor node and re-add it with the mainline leds-pwm binding, so
each channel gets native PWM-resolution brightness (0-255) at
/sys/class/leds/{red,green,blue} with no dithering.

The LED power rail is gated by gpio4 RK_PC7: the vendor driver drove that pin
high in its probe() to power the ring (and low to cut it). leds-pwm has no
concept of an enable GPIO, so hog the pin high at boot instead. Confirmed on
hardware: with the pin high, all three channels light in the correct colors;
with it low (leds-pwm's default), the ring stays dark regardless of PWM duty.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576s-r157-v2.0-wf1019-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576s-r157-v2.0-wf1019-linux.dts
@@ -829,3 +829,50 @@
 &wdt {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * RGB light ring: the base rk3576s-evb-r157.dtsi describes this LED with the
+ * out-of-tree "pwm-four-leds" driver (/dev/ledjni, 16 levels per channel).
+ * Replace that node with the mainline leds-pwm binding for native 0-255
+ * brightness per channel at /sys/class/leds/{red,green,blue} (no userspace
+ * dithering). The pwm2 channels (ch6=red @2ade6000, ch2=green @2ade2000,
+ * ch5=blue @2ade5000) are already enabled on the m1 pin mux by evb-r157.dtsi.
+ *
+ * The LED power rail is gated by gpio4 RK_PC7: the vendor driver drove it high
+ * in probe() to enable the ring. leds-pwm has no notion of an enable GPIO, so
+ * hog that pin high at boot instead.
+ */
+&gpio4 {
+	led_ring_power_hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <RK_PC7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "led-ring-power";
+	};
+};
+
+/ {
+	/delete-node/ pwmleds;
+
+	pwmleds {
+		compatible = "pwm-leds";
+
+		led_ring_red {
+			label = "red";
+			pwms = <&pwm2_8ch_6 0 1000000 0>;
+			max-brightness = <255>;
+		};
+
+		led_ring_green {
+			label = "green";
+			pwms = <&pwm2_8ch_2 0 1000000 0>;
+			max-brightness = <255>;
+		};
+
+		led_ring_blue {
+			label = "blue";
+			pwms = <&pwm2_8ch_5 0 1000000 0>;
+			max-brightness = <255>;
+		};
+	};
+};
